---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/data';
const installer = 'java -jar neoforge-installer.jar --installServer';
const heap = '-Xms4G\n-Xmx8G';
const hostingCode = 'Mika';
const hostingLink = 'https://www.bisecthosting.com/mika';
---
<Layout title="Dedicated server setup" description="Install a matching NeoForge server, preserve Towns & Kingdoms content and keep a recoverable world.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Guides / Multiplayer</p>
  <h1>Set up a dedicated server</h1>
  <p class="intro">Host your own Towns &amp; Kingdoms 3 world and keep the server and clients on the same pack build.</p>
  <aside id="hosting" class="callout hosting-option" aria-labelledby="hosting-title">
    <div>
      <h2 id="hosting-title">Host with BisectHosting</h2>
      <p>Use code <strong><code>{hostingCode}</code></strong> at checkout when you rent a server for your group.</p>
      <p class="affiliate-note">The pack creator may earn a commission from purchases through this link.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="button" href={hostingLink} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener">View BisectHosting plans</a>
  </aside>
  <nav class="toc-inline" aria-label="Server setup steps"><a href="#files">Pack files</a><a href="#java">Java</a><a href="#install">NeoForge</a><a href="#parity">Content parity</a><a href="#launch">First launch</a><a href="#operations">Running the world</a></nav>
  <div class="prose">
    <section id="files"><p class="eyebrow section">01 / Prepare</p><h2>Choose the matching files</h2><p>Obtain the <strong>Towns & Kingdoms 3: Beyond the Forge</strong> file supplied for your installation. The <a href="https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/modpacks/towns-kingdoms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">official CurseForge project</a> covers multiple editions, so check the edition and exact pack file before downloading. A TK2 server archive belongs to another Minecraft installation.</p><p>Use the matching dedicated server package when one is provided. If you have only a launcher export, obtain the server installation instructions through the <a href="https://discord.gg/CRYk3uDPVt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">official Discord</a>. A manifest ZIP is an installation description, not a ready-to-run server, and a client mod folder can contain renderers or menu mods that do not belong on a dedicated server.</p><p>Create an empty server directory. For an existing world, stop the old server and take a complete backup before replacing any files.</p></section>
    <section id="java"><p class="eyebrow section">02 / Runtime</p><h2>Check the server’s Java runtime</h2><p>For Minecraft 1.21.1, NeoForge’s baseline is 64-bit Java 21. Use the runtime specified by your dedicated server package if it gives one. Check the Java executable used by your server panel or start script.</p><div class="command"><pre><code>java -version</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy-code="java -version" aria-label="Copy Java version command">Copy</button></div><p>If several Java versions are installed, select the required executable in the host panel or by its full path in the start script.</p></section>
    <section id="install"><p class="eyebrow section">03 / Loader</p><h2>Install NeoForge</h2><p>If your server package supplies startup scripts, follow its instructions. For a manual loader installation, download the installer for the NeoForge version listed in your pack profile from the <a href="https://projects.neoforged.net/neoforged/neoforge" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NeoForge downloads page</a>. Save it as <code>neoforge-installer.jar</code> in the server directory and run it from there.</p><div class="command"><pre><code>{installer}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy-code={installer} aria-label="Copy NeoForge installation command">Copy</button></div><p>The installer creates <code>run.sh</code>, <code>run.bat</code>, <code>user_jvm_args.txt</code> and the loader libraries. Keep those generated files together. Use the loader required by the pack instead of substituting an unrelated newer build.</p></section>
    <section id="parity"><p class="eyebrow section">04 / Pack content</p><h2>Keep the common content together</h2><p>Install the dedicated package’s content, configuration and data as instructed. Preserve the complete common KubeJS structure: <code>startup_scripts</code>, <code>server_scripts</code>, <code>config</code>, <code>pack_data</code> and <code>data</code>. Custom items registered at startup must match the clients.</p><p>Keep shared mod configuration and any supplied <code>defaultconfigs</code> alongside the matching mods. Client assets and client scripts remain on the clients. Do not remove a content mod because its name sounds visual; use the server package’s supplied list or the mod’s documented environment.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Content</th><th scope="col">What must stay in step</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Content mods and custom registrations</td><td>Matching common mods and KubeJS startup definitions</td></tr><tr><td>Recipes, tags, loot and weapon capabilities</td><td>The matching server scripts, <code>pack_data</code> and <code>kubejs/data</code></td></tr><tr><td>Textures, models, trails and client UI</td><td>The matching client assets and client-side installation</td></tr><tr><td>World and per-world configuration</td><td>Preserve the existing world and its configuration during updates</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section id="launch"><p class="eyebrow section">05 / First start</p><h2>Launch and accept the EULA</h2><p>Start with <code>./run.sh</code> on Linux or <code>.\run.bat</code> on Windows. Read the <a href="https://www.minecraft.net/eula" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Minecraft EULA</a> and, if you agree, set <code>eula=true</code> in <code>eula.txt</code>, then start again.</p><p>Set the Java heap in <code>user_jvm_args.txt</code>. The following is an example allocation, not a statement of the host’s total RAM:</p><div class="command"><pre><code>{heap}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy-code={heap} aria-label="Copy example Java heap settings">Copy</button></div><p>Leave memory for the operating system and Java’s non-heap allocations. Watch actual use before changing the limit. Wait for the server’s <code>Done</code> message and check the first-start log for missing mods or failed scripts.</p><p>Keep <code>online-mode=true</code> for a normal authenticated server. Enable a whitelist for a private group. Use the game port configured in <code>server.properties</code>; the default is TCP 25565. Open only the required game port in the host and network firewall.</p></section>
    <section id="operations"><p class="eyebrow section">06 / Keep the world healthy</p><h2>Test before inviting everyone</h2><ol><li><strong>Join with a matching client.</strong> Confirm that custom items, recipes and the character systems appear without registry errors.</li><li><strong>Test a small shared workshop.</strong> Craft a basic component, use a weapon and identify a piece of equipment before importing large builds.</li><li><strong>Back up a recoverable installation.</strong> Keep the world, its server configuration, pack configuration and KubeJS content together. Test the restore process on a separate copy.</li><li><strong>Update the whole required set.</strong> Stop the server, follow the patch’s merge or replacement instructions, update clients and fully restart. Keep the previous working backup until the update has been tested.</li><li><strong>Measure a slowdown.</strong> Note what was running and collect the relevant logs or a Spark profile. Change one cause at a time.</li></ol><p>For access to an official world, use the <a href={href('servers/')}>official servers page</a>. For an installation failure, collect the logs described in <a href={href('support/#logs')}>the support guide</a>.</p><p class="reference-link">Platform reference: <a href="https://docs.neoforged.net/user/docs/server/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NeoForge server installation</a> · <a href="https://docs.neoforged.net/user/docs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Java requirements</a></p></section>
  </div><p id="command-feedback" class="copy-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-code]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const feedback = document.getElementById('command-feedback');
      try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copyCode || ''); if (feedback) feedback.textContent = 'Command copied.'; }
      catch { if (feedback) feedback.textContent = 'Select the command text and copy it.'; }
    }));
  </script>
</Layout>
<style>
  .hosting-option {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 14px 24px;
    max-width: 74ch;
  }
  .hosting-option h2 { color: var(--text); font-size: 19px; margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .hosting-option p { margin: 0; }
  .hosting-option .affiliate-note { font-size: 13px; margin-top: 5px; }
  .command{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:16px;padding:16px 18px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:7px;background:var(--surface);margin:18px 0}.command pre{margin:0;flex:1;min-width:0;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;line-height:1.7}.command button{font-size:13px;flex-shrink:0}.prose .reference-link{font-size:14px}.copy-feedback{min-height:24px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.prose section{scroll-margin-top:95px}@media(max-width:550px){.command{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:9px;padding:12px}.command pre code{font-size:14px}}
</style>
